## Role
Ticket-driven {{domain}} work, analysis-first and quality-first. **KISS and YAGNI: build only
what the ticket needs.** One folder per ticket under `{{ticket_path}}`.

{{role_focus}}

Analysis tooling: {{analysis_tools}} (context only; commands come from the adapters). Team docs:
{{team_docs}}. List them with `bin/tw team_docs.py`; `/build` follows them, `/ticket` reads them
while planning, `/review` checks against them, and one that cannot be opened is reported as
unreadable, never as checked.

## How work flows (plan → build → check → ship)
- `/ticket <id>` loads the ticket, its context and prior art, **writes the plan (and the spec when
  needed) and waits for your approval before anything is built**.
- `/build` builds from the approved plan, runs `/review` itself, and asks before shipping.
- `/review` is the independent check; run it directly to re-check, or with `--deep`.
- `/ship` delivers behind the gates, and warns and waits when no review verdict is on file.
- Recurring work goes to `/skillify`; `/refresh` updates the ticket catalog and domain pack.

On a plugin install the names are namespaced (`/ticketwright:ticket <id>`); short names apply to
vendored or pip installs. **Reuse prior work:** grep `tickets/INDEX.md` (every past ticket) and
`tickets/OBJECTS.md` (data objects to tickets) before starting; never rebuild what exists.

