## Your machine, your settings
Everyone's machine is set up differently, and that is expected. Per-person settings (connections,
local folders such as the Drive mount, the apps that open deliverables for review, and who you
are) live in git-ignored `.claude/config/*.local.yaml` files that `/setup` writes for each person;
`people/<id>.yaml` holds the committed, portable part. Never commit a `*.local.yaml` file.
**New to this repo?** After cloning, install the plugin (below), restart, then run
`/ticketwright:setup --teammate` to write your own settings.

## Installing this plugin
Registering the marketplace is not installing the plugin — a teammate who opens and trusts the
repo gets the marketplace clone, then runs the install themselves (Track 2). An agent helping
someone install can be handed this:

```text
Install the Ticketwright plugin for this repo. Start with:
python3 ~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/ticketwright/bin/plugin_doctor.py
Follow its fixes in order. I want it installed for this repo only, not globally.
If a check fails in a way its fix doesn't cover, stop and tell me instead of
working around it. When it's clean, tell me how to restart.
```

```bash
claude plugin marketplace add https://github.com/kyle-chalmers/ticketwright.git --scope project
claude plugin install ticketwright@ticketwright --scope project
```

The safety hooks ship with the plugin: until it is installed and the session restarted, nothing
below is enforced mechanically. Full checklist: <https://github.com/kyle-chalmers/ticketwright/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md>.

## Permissions
**No permission needed:** read queries, data exploration, repo files, local analysis and output.
**Ask first:** high-risk DB writes; commits, pushes and PRs; tracker comments; chat messages;
docstore backups. **DB-write protocol:** show the exact SQL, explain the change, wait for `yes`,
then run; how much is gated is `policies.db_write_requires_approval`, so read it before assuming.
**Raw meeting transcripts:** ask before staging one from `source_materials/` for commit or copying
it into a docstore backup; commit only the curated `*-meeting.md` summary. The hooks see shell
commands only: SQL sent through a warehouse MCP server is not gated, so run warehouse writes
through the CLI. The agent reference's enforcement table says which gates are mechanical where.

## On other agent runtimes
Claude Code runs the plugin's hooks for you. Other agents read this file but load nothing else
on their own, so on those:
- **No session-start hook** (Codex CLI, Devin, Cursor, Antigravity, OpenCode): at session start run
  `bash "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || echo .)/bin/tw" hook_shim.py --runtime <name> --hook session_context`, then the same with `--hook ticket_index_context`.
- **No index-refresh hook** (all but Claude Code and Antigravity): after changing a ticket, run
  `bash "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || echo .)/bin/tw" build_ticket_index.py`.
- **Guards not wired** (Codex CLI and Devin until wired by hand, Cline): nothing stops a DB write, a
  raw transcript commit or an unreviewed push, so the rules above are yours to follow.
- **Deny-only runtimes** (Codex CLI, Devin, OpenCode): a denied statement names a one-shot
  re-approval; use it only after the person says yes to that statement.
- List warehouse connections by name only; never print a list showing account, user or role.

## Team policies (values in `stack.yaml`; full text in the agent reference)
1. **hard_halt_before_external_posts**: pause for a human go before any tracker, chat or docstore write, or a push or PR of a ticket without an approved review.
2. **db_write_requires_approval**: `off` | `high_risk` (default) | `all`. `high_risk` gates `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, `DELETE`, `UPDATE`, `MERGE`, `GRANT`/`REVOKE`, every `CREATE OR REPLACE`, every `ALTER` except `ALTER … ADD`, and anything unrecognized; plain `CREATE`, `INSERT INTO`, `ALTER … ADD` and `COMMENT ON` run without asking. `all` gates every mutation.
3. **chat_default_draft**: draft, don't send, unless told "send it".
4. **hyperlink_everything**: every ticket id, file and PR is a link.
5. **skillify_everything**: recurring work becomes a skill. Before ending a session that worked a ticket and did not reach `/ship`'s retro, follow the repeat check in the kit's `.claude/skills/skillify/repeats.md` and close with one line: the `/skillify` suggestion, the skill that already does it, or nothing. Never run `/skillify` unasked.
6. **reduce_assumptions**: ask before building; document every assumption in the ticket README.
7. **commit_plan_before_implement**: `/ticket` commits the plan before `/build` runs.
8. **system_evolution**: a failure fixes the AI layer (rule, context, skill or adapter), not just the ticket.
9. **deterministic_outputs**: explicit `ORDER BY` on exports.
10. **human_review_handoff**: `off` | `review` (default) | `all`; open deliverables with `bash "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || echo .)/bin/tw" handoff.sh <paths>` and wait for sign-off. No viewer config: say so once and carry on.
11. **ship_merges_pr**: `true` (default) means `/ship` asks once more, then squash-merges the PR.

## Ticket folder
```
{{ticket_path}}/
├── README.md            # business context + ALL assumptions + QC results
├── source_materials/    # attachments / inputs
├── final_deliverables/  # numbered in review order; filenames carry record counts
├── qc_queries/          # numbered QC + the /review verdict
└── exploratory_analysis/
```

## Deliverables, quality and communication
**ASCII punctuation only in cell values** of CSV exports (no em or en dashes, smart quotes or
ellipses); header row first, record count in the filename. Every deliverable climbs the pyramid:
① dialect lint → ② counts and dedup → ③ cross-source reconciliation → ④ independent re-run →
⑤ human sign-off. `/ship` waits for a typed `ship unreviewed` when no review is on file.

Word limits: tracker comment <{{wl_tracker_comment}} · chat <{{wl_chat}} · PR <{{wl_pr}} · new
ticket <{{wl_ticket}}>. Tracker comments are business-first and link the docstore file. Chat:
include {{chat_always_include}}; link everything. A voice profile shapes drafts, never the limits.

## Git
Branch = ticket id off `{{default_branch}}`. Semantic commits and PRs. Stage only files you
changed; Co-Authored-By trailer on commits. Repo-setup files (`.claude/settings.json`,
`stack.yaml`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.gitignore`) get their own `chore(plugins): …` commit on
the ticket's branch, never folded into the feature commit.
